From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Project Luma <engineering@projectluma.org>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 22:22:02 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] LumaUI Settings: a GNOME panel keeps the phone's status
 inset

On a phone the window bleeds under the status bar and a LumaUI page
places its own title island below it. A page still drawn by its GNOME
panel (Mobile Network, Printers) had no such inset: its header bar sat in
the status bar row, title and switch under the clock and indicators, in
every way the panel was opened. The panel host now keeps the status
bar's height clear on a phone. Computers and LumaUI pages are unchanged.
---
 shell/luma-settings.css | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/shell/luma-settings.css b/shell/luma-settings.css
index 5118dec..b0e1828 100644
--- a/shell/luma-settings.css
+++ b/shell/luma-settings.css
@@ -145,6 +145,9 @@ button.cf-crumb image { -gtk-icon-size: 12px; }
   border: none; outline: none; color: @luma_muted; }
 .cf-panel-host headerbar button.image-button:hover, .cf-panel-host headerbar button.back:hover { background: @luma_hover; color: @luma_ink; }
 .cf-panel-host headerbar button image { -gtk-icon-size: 16px; }
+/* A phone: the window bleeds under the status bar and a LumaUI page sets its title island below it.
+ * A GNOME panel's header bar has no such inset, so its host keeps the status bar's height clear. */
+window.lumaui-phone-device.lumaui-bleed .cf-panel-host { padding-top: var(--lumaui-phone-frame-status); }
 
 .cf-card {
   background: @luma_well;
